# [ADAPT: Project Name] — Project Governance Rules

## 🧭 NATURAL-LANGUAGE ROUTER

When the user states a goal, route it to explicit NAOS commands instead of
guessing hidden automation:

- New project -> `naos adopt . --mode greenfield --profile <profile> --dry-run`
- Existing repo -> `naos adopt . --mode brownfield --profile <profile> --dry-run`
- Daily task -> `/naos-d-start` then `/naos-task-start <TASK-ID>`
- PR/release review -> `naos gate-evaluate`, `naos evidence-pack`, `naos dashboard`
- Governance-surface change -> `naos systemic-impact`, `naos control-plane-review`

Keep commands visible. Reports are review evidence, not approval.

## 🔒 RULE #1: DATA PRIVACY GOVERNANCE

### Define Your Restricted Schemas

[ADAPT: Replace this with your data isolation model]

**Example (multi-tenant SaaS)**:
- ✅ `[TENANT_DB]` — PII storage ALLOWED (encrypted, per-tenant)
- ❌ `[DISCOVERY_LAYER]` — PII storage FORBIDDEN

**Forbidden in restricted schemas:**
- Full name (first_name, last_name, full_name)
- Email address (email, contact_email)
- Phone number (phone, mobile, telephone)
- Physical address (street, city, zip, postal_code)
- Government IDs (ssn, passport, driver_license)
- IP addresses (if tied to individual)

**Safe identifiers:**
- ✅ Organization UUID / tenant_id
- ✅ Company name (not person name)
- ✅ Aggregated statistics
- ✅ Cryptographic hashes

If PII detected in restricted paths → **STOP! FIX BEFORE COMMIT!**

